    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0418" n="302" xml:id="pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1490.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Dominican Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dominican Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 1, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to send you
                    herewith a copy of the Gaceta Official No. 2569, of January 2, 1915, which
                    contains the decree<anchor n="6" xml:id="d285-f1"/> dated December 26, 1914, by
                    which President Jiménes forbade the use of the stamps and stamped paper that
                    formed part of the internal revenue of the Dominican Republic.</p>
                <p>I respectfully call your attention to the fact that that first step toward the
                    rehabilitation of the internal revenues is taken in accordance with the State
                    Department’s suggestions in the memorandum of January 8 [9], 1915, and the
                    telegram sent to Mr. Sullivan on the 12th of the same month.</p>
                <p>I renew [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Enrique Jiménez</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
